    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023-sch-1-sec-36b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36B Cessation of citizenship if citizenship cessation order made by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023#sch-1-sec-36b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "court etc.\n\n(1) Subject to this section, if an order is made under subsection 36C(1)\nin relation to a person, the person ceases to be an Australian citizen\nat the time the order is made.\nOrder overturned or quashed\n\n(2) If a decision of a court overturns or quashes the order made under\nsubsection 36C(1), the person’s citizenship is taken never to have\nceased under subsection (1) of this section.\n\n(3) The validity of anything done in reliance on the order made under\nsubsection 36C(1) before the order was overturned or quashed is\nnot affected.\nAppeal decision\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a decision (the first decision) of a court overturning or\nquashing the order made under subsection 36C(1) in relation\nto the person is appealed; and\n\n(b) the decision (the second decision) on appeal overturns or\nquashes the first decision;\nthe person ceases to be an Australian citizen at the time the second\ndecision is made.",
      "skos:definition": "court etc.\n\n(1) Subject to this section, if an order is made under subsection 36C(1)\nin relation to a person, the person ceases to be an Australian citizen\nat the time the order is made.\nOrder overturned or quashed\n\n(2) If a decision of a court overturns or quashes the order made under\nsubsection 36C(1), the person’s citizenship is taken never to have\nceased under subsection (1) of this section.\n\n(3) The validity of anything done in reliance on the order made under\nsubsection 36C(1) before the order was overturned or quashed is\nnot affected.\nAppeal decision\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a decision (the first decision) of a court overturning or\nquashing the order made under subsection 36C(1) in relation\nto the person is appealed; and\n\n(b) the decision (the second decision) on appeal overturns or\nquashes the first decision;\nthe person ceases to be an Australian citizen at the time the second\ndecision is made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "271841c098d5905fb787437234078e1acddc049b8e570094d0e1632eeaff8965"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-repudiation-act-2023#sch-1-sec-36b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36B Cessation of citizenship if citizenship cessation order made by",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "court etc.\n\n(1) Subject to this section, if an order is made under subsection 36C(1)\nin relation to a person, the person ceases to be an Australian citizen\nat the time the order is made.\nOrder overturned or quashed\n\n(2) If a decision of a court overturns or quashes the order made under\nsubsection 36C(1), the person’s citizenship is taken never to have\nceased under subsection (1) of this section.\n\n(3) The validity of anything done in reliance on the order made under\nsubsection 36C(1) before the order was overturned or quashed is\nnot affected.\nAppeal decision\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a decision (the first decision) of a court overturning or\nquashing the order made under subsection 36C(1) in relation\nto the person is appealed; and\n\n(b) the decision (the second decision) on appeal overturns or\nquashes the first decision;\nthe person ceases to be an Australian citizen at the time the second\ndecision is made."
    },
